Ingested collections live here — one folder per collection under data/datasets/,
plus data/appstate/ for the accounts database in the public profile.

This directory is a BIND MOUNT, not a Docker volume, so `docker compose down -v`
cannot delete it. Back it up by copying the folder; move an installation by moving it.

Set DATA_DIR in your .env to keep the data somewhere else (another disk, a faster
filesystem). The default is this folder.
